--- /dev/null
+++ b/.claude/skills/freebsd-port/spec.org
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+#+TITLE: claude skill freebsd-port
+
+- disable model invocation
+- base work off an up-to-date copy of ports tree
+  - ports tree is cloned from public upstream, into a dir in
+    =/var/tmp/=
+- create a new port from user provided info, or update an existing
+  port
+- research ports tree for similar ports to determine patterns
+- look at upstream / dist sites etc to use the latest good version
+  - newest released version from release page or registry, not just tags
+  - exclude yanked versions
+  - exclude pre releases
+- run all the linters to make sure it's clean
+- prepare the patch only - do not build, it will take too long
+  - getting metadata is okay, e.g. make fetch, make makesum
+- post patch to list with [freebsd-ports PATCH] prefix
+  - patch will be applied with =git am= in a git dir, no need to be
+    supported by =just am=
+- completely independent skill, does not use portia. Can refer to
+  portia for useful ideas to integrate into the skill
